Privileged access obtained                    impact       high    A principal was given a privileged role or permission. Treat what it governs as under attacker control until reviewed.
Persistence established                       impact       high    A way back in was created: a credential, a run key, a task or a service. Access survives a password reset.
Valid identity used                           impact       high    The attacker signed in as an identity that exists. Sign-in controls did not stop it.
Data collected                                impact       high    Mail, chat or documents were read in bulk. Treat their content as disclosed. Affected: alice@corp.example, bob@corp.example.
Environment mapped                            impact       low     Identities, resources or configuration were listed. Later steps were probably aimed with the result.
Revoke sessions and reset identities          remediation  high    Revoke the sessions and tokens of every identity in the evidence and reset its credentials.
Remove added credentials                      remediation  high    Remove every password and key added to an application or service principal, then review all credentials added since the first step.
Remove role and permission grants             remediation  high    Remove the role assignments and application permissions that were granted, then review every privileged member and consent.
Scope the data taken                          remediation  high    Establish from audit logs which mailboxes, chats, sites and files were read or sent out, and assess that data as breached.
Follow what was enumerated                    remediation  low     Use what was listed to predict targets: check those identities, vaults and hosts for later activity.
Restrict application credentials and consent  mitigation   medium  Limit who may add a credential or grant a permission to an application, and alert when either happens.
Guard privileged roles                        mitigation   medium  Require approval and raise an alert for every privileged role assignment, and keep standing membership small.
Watch application access to mail and files    mitigation   low     Alert on an application that is granted mail or file permissions, and on one that reads them in volume.
